# Siblings the CI gate checks out (at their canonical origin head) next to this
# repo so the encoder's cross-repo byte-identity guards resolve them
# deterministically.
#
# xchain-hub: test/unit/coins-conformance.test.js compares src/coins against the
# canonical ../xchain-hub/src/coins.
#
# xchain-documentation: test/unit/ActionManifestConformance.test.js compares the
# vendored manifest against ../xchain-documentation/protocol/action-manifest.json.
#
# Both SKIP when the sibling is absent, which is right for a standalone deploy
# but was a trap on a shared venue : $CI_ROOT/work kept a checkout per
# repo ever gated there, so an undeclared sibling was not absent at all, it was
# whatever revision another repo's run had left behind, and the guard silently
# compared against that. This repo was the original casualty - a 2026-07-25 push
# went red here against hub dad518a and reported drift in the OPPOSITE direction
# from the real one, while the same commit passed on test-host. Declaring them makes
# the harness ship canonical and rm -rf any leftover.
xchain-hub
xchain-documentation
